    ============================================================================
    PROFILE COMPLETION NUDGE POPUP + NOTIFICATION BUG FIX
    ============================================================================

    ============================================================================
    1. PROFILE COMPLETION + NOTIFICATION POPUP  (#profileNudgeOverlay)
    ============================================================================
    Location : templates/p_struct.html  (inherited by ALL premium pages)
    z-index  : 9500  (above promoCard 9200, below nothing critical)
    Delay    : 3500ms after DOMContentLoaded

    HOW IT WORKS:
    - After 3.5s the JS calls /api/check-profile (GET, requires auth)
    - Simultaneously checks window.PushNotifications.init() for subscription state
    - Decision logic:
        • profile_completed === false  →  show Step 1 (Complete Profile)
        • profile done + notifications not enabled + not blocked  →  show Step 2 (Enable Notifications)
        • everything done  →  do nothing
    - Snooze: dismissing stores a 24-hour timestamp in localStorage
      Key: 'abhihub_profile_nudge_snooze'
    - Notification done flag: 'abhihub_notif_nudge_done' (set on successful subscribe)

    STEP 1 — Complete Profile:
        Header : violet→blue gradient + 👤 emoji (bouncing)
        Body   : animated progress bar (30% if incomplete, 100% if complete)
                 3 feature bullets (college/dept, year, verified badge)
        CTA    : "Complete Profile Now 🚀"  →  href="/account"
        Skip   : "Enable notifications instead →"  →  switches to Step 2

    STEP 2 — Enable Notifications:
        Header : teal→blue→violet gradient + 🔔 emoji (bouncing)
        Body   : 3 bullets (new papers, rank alerts, upload approved)
        CTA    : "Enable Notifications 🔔"  →  calls PushNotifications.subscribe()
                 Button states: Enabling... / ✅ enabled / ⚠️ error messages
        Skip   : "Maybe later"  →  dismisses with 24h snooze

    Closes on backdrop click (same 24h snooze).

    GLOBAL FUNCTIONS (window.*):
        dismissProfileNudge()        — close + 24h snooze
        nudgeGoToStep2()             — switch from step 1 → step 2
        nudgeEnableNotifications()   — async; calls PushNotifications.subscribe()

    ============================================================================
    2. NOTIFICATION BUG FIXES
    ============================================================================

    BUG 1 — Key mismatch in send_notification / is_user_subscribed
    ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    File    : push_notifications.py
    Root cause: get_all_push_subscriptions() returns a dict keyed by USER UUID
                but send_notification() and is_user_subscribed() were looking up
                by email string  →  always "User not subscribed".

    Fix:
        - send_notification(user_id, ...) now expects a UUID (not email)
        - Subscription info is extracted from sub_data dict correctly
        - On 410/404 expiry, uses remove_subscription_by_endpoint(endpoint)
          instead of the broken remove_subscription(user_id) (which expected email)
        - Default url changed from '/premium' → '/dashboard'
        - is_user_subscribed() docstring updated to clarify UUID requirement

    BUG 2 — /api/push/status used email, looked up UUID dict
    ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    File    : push_api.py
    Root cause: status() route passed email to is_user_subscribed(), which
                checks presence in UUID-keyed dict → always returns False.

    Fix in status():
        - Reads user_uid from session['user']['uid'] first
        - Falls back to Supabase lookup (profiles table) if uid missing
        - Passes resolved UUID to is_user_subscribed()

    BUG 3 — subscribe() route used email but add_subscription expects email
    ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
    push_api.py subscribe() → calls add_subscription(user_email, subscription)
    save_push_subscription(user_email, ...) looks up UUID from email internally.
    This was already correct; variable just renamed for clarity.

    ============================================================================
    3. API ENDPOINTS INVOLVED
    ============================================================================
    GET  /api/check-profile         → returns { profile_completed: bool }
    GET  /api/push/vapid-public-key → returns { publicKey: str }
    POST /api/push/subscribe        → body: { subscription: {...} }
    GET  /api/push/status           → returns { enabled: bool, subscribed: bool }
    DELETE /api/push/unsubscribe    → unsubscribes current user

